WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.042
Welcome to our instructional video on setting up the operating workspace for a practice route.

2
00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:14.083
Today, we'll create the minimum essentials to simulate a full day of operations, from planning to delivery confirmation.

3
00:00:14.083 --> 00:00:21.125
We won't migrate every record, just enough to prove a complete workflow.

4
00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:27.650
Let's start in the Settings menu.

5
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:34.175
Ensure your organization's name, service timezone, primary depot, support contact, and customer-facing information are accurate.

6
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:40.700
The timezone is crucial as it affects appointment windows, planned arrivals, tracking, and event history.

7
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.895
Invite users with the least privileged role they need.

8
00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:51.090
Owners and Admins manage the organization.

9
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:56.285
Dispatchers plan, publish, assign, dispatch, and resolve route changes.

10
00:00:56.285 --> 00:01:01.480
Drivers use the mobile execution flow for their assigned work.

11
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:06.675
Viewers can inspect dashboards, tracking, proof, and reports without altering operational records.

12
00:01:06.675 --> 00:01:13.375
Create a pilot Driver and verify their details.

13
00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:20.075
This includes name, phone, email, license information, employment status, and any required certifications.

14
00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:26.775
Then, create an available vehicle with realistic weight, volume, pallet, equipment, territory, and driver eligibility rules.

15
00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:33.475
Inaccurate capacity can hinder the practice route's realism.

16
00:01:33.475 --> 00:01:39.975
Add or import only the customers needed for the pilot route.

17
00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:46.475
Verify their service addresses, contacts, receiver hours, site restrictions, and special instructions.

18
00:01:46.475 --> 00:01:52.975
Never include passwords, tokens, or private access instructions in spreadsheets or support requests.

19
00:01:52.975 --> 00:01:59.475
Sensitive access codes should only be entered in the approved secure field.

20
00:01:59.475 --> 00:02:04.544
Once done, check the Academy readiness card.

21
00:02:04.544 --> 00:02:09.613
Ensure the depot, active Driver, and ready vehicle steps are complete.

22
00:02:09.613 --> 00:02:14.681
If any step remains incomplete, open its action and correct the underlying record.

23
00:02:14.681 --> 00:02:19.750
Then, complete the knowledge check before proceeding to Route Operations.

24
00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:25.880
Before moving forward, pause and verify the saved records.

25
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:32.010
Open the depot, user list, Driver, vehicle, and pilot customers.

26
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:38.140
Check status, role, timezone, capacity, contact, and instruction fields one more time.

27
00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:44.270
This preventive measure ensures smooth operations and avoids false routing blockers during the practice day.

28
00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:50.400
Return to the Academy only when the readiness card reflects the real setup.
